========================================================================
Research takeaways
========================================================================
1. The unit-distance analogue of S646 is a fixed Moser layer
   quantum: after the cap transient, every added slab contributes
   the same direction vector with total 27 edges.
2. The 27 quantum splits as 8 spine edges plus 19 hidden bulk
   edges.  A point-order tournament can forget this split; a proof
   carrier should retain it.
3. At n=21 and n=22, pure-bulk direction mass equals the spine
   length.  That marks the current frontier as a balanced section/
   bulk fixed pocket, not just a high edge count.
4. The next no-leak target is cap-endpoint conservativity: a
   hypothetical 61-edge n=22 row must repair the degree-3 cap
   endpoint or leave the fixed Moser carrier.
